 "headline": "On 200 CODEBRIM images, Drishyam at a 30% pixel cap found 0.20 of ground-truth boxes using 0.29 of the image's pixels, versus 0.21 for 20%-overlap 512-px tiling using 1.62: 0.96x its recall (95% CI 0.86-1.06, 0.82x with one-box-per-class boxes, 1.86x with as-specified mixed boxes) at 0.18x its pixels, which meets the 0.9x-at-0.3x hypothesis on the point estimate, but the 95% CI includes values below 0.9. It is 0.99x a single 1024-px downscale (95% CI 0.91-1.08, 0.20 at 0.07 of the pixels), 0.89x L1 tiling (0.22 at 0.42, the best grid) and 0.92x L2 tiling (0.21 at 0.10), and 1.54x L0 tiling when a match needs IoU >= 0.3 (95% CI 1.25-1.92, no contains-the-centre clause); its own boxes placed at random would score 0.12 (0.03 with IoU only)."
